   "type": "Feature",
   "properties": {
    "project_name": "UCSF Medical Center at Mission Bay",
    "site": "Mission Bay South",
    "status": "complete",
    "use": "institutional",
    "geometry_type": "real",
    "digitized_from": "DataSF Assessor parcels (acdm-wktn), lots 8723008, 3992003, 8724001 and 8729001 (mapped 1998-07-01, 2001-03-20, 2006-05-24; active), joined into one outline; the earlier outline came from: OpenStreetMap (way 580277612, name=UCSF Medical Center at Mission Bay, amenity=hospital, operator=University of California San Francisco, 1975 4th St)",
    "digitization_method": "ADDED 2026-09-18 for Mission Bay's UCSF campus pass: real OSM building footprint for the main hospital complex, which houses UCSF Benioff Children's Hospital, UCSF Bakar Cancer Hospital and Betty Irene Moore Women's Hospital under one roof. 2026-10-02: public-text pass. accuracy_caveat reworded for readers (meaning unchanged; no change to the shape, status, use or geometry_type); previous wording -- accuracy_caveat: 'REAL -- surveyed OpenStreetMap building footprint, not a hand trace or plan estimate. This is the opposite situation from Mission Bay's condo-mapped residential towers (Avalon, Radiance, etc.): here, ONE large Assessor land parcel spans SEVERAL UCSF buildings (confirmed against data/raw/parcels.geojson and DataSF's Assessor tax roll -- e.g. blklot 8711507 alone is about 12-13 acres: 675 Nelson Rising Ln with a lot area of 572,576 sq ft (13.1 acres) on the Assessor roll, 675 Mission Bay Blvd and 12.2 acres in DataSF's Parcels layer, far larger than any single building on it), so using the parcel boundary per building would make multiple records overlap and double-count the same ground. The real building footprint is the only non-overlapping, honest shape for each one.'. REPLACED 2026-10-12 (shape; status and use unchanged): the owner approved building records whose outline matches an Assessor lot at 85% or better, both ways, using the lot (CLAUDE.md, 'An official parcel beats our drawing'). DataSF's Assessor layer (data/raw/parcels.geojson) has the union of Assessor lots 8723008, 3992003, 8724001 and 8729001 (59,505 m2, active, mapped 1998-07-01, 2001-03-20, 2006-05-24); the earlier outline of 59,028 m2 and the lot overlap with IoU 0.87 (94% of the earlier outline lies inside the lot and it covers 93% of the lot). The outline is now their union using the lots' own vertices (no simplification). geometry_type stays 'real'. Previous digitized_from: 'OpenStreetMap (way 580277612, name=UCSF Medical Center at Mission Bay, amenity=hospital, operator=University of California San Francisco, 1975 4th St)'. Previous accuracy_caveat: 'REAL -- surveyed OpenStreetMap building footprint, not a hand trace or plan estimate. This is the opposite situation from Mission Bay's condo-mapped residential towers (Avalon, Radiance, etc.): here, ONE large Assessor land parcel spans SEVERAL UCSF buildings (confirmed against DataSF's Assessor parcel data and tax roll -- e.g. blklot 8711507 alone is about 12-13 acres: 675 Nelson Rising Ln with a lot area of 572,576 sq ft (13.1 acres) on the Assessor roll, 675 Mission Bay Blvd and 12.2 acres in DataSF's Parcels layer, far larger than any single building on it), so using the parcel boundary per building would make multiple records overlap and double-count the same ground. The real building footprint is the only non-overlapping, honest shape for each one.'.",
    "accuracy_caveat": "REAL lot geometry -- the outline is the union of Assessor lots 8723008, 3992003, 8724001 and 8729001 (59,505 m2, active), so its edges are recorded lot lines, not a surveyed building footprint: it includes any yard, setback or plaza inside the lot and can sit a little off the walls. Until 2026-10-12 this record showed the surveyed building footprint (OpenStreetMap (way 580277612, name=UCSF Medical Center at Mission Bay, amenity=hospital, operator=University of California San Francisco, 1975 4th St)); 94% of that outline lies inside the lot and it covered 93% of the lot. The outline has two parts because lot 8723008 (601 16th St) does not touch the others. That these four lots are the hospital's own is Pier & Point's inference from location, shape and size (each lies at least 90% inside the earlier outline); no source read ties the lot numbers to the hospital. Four other lots lie mostly inside the earlier outline and are left out, because nothing read ties them to it: 8728001 (770 Mariposa St) and 3943001, 3943003 and 3943007 (1800 and 1830 3rd St). Other UCSF buildings in Mission Bay stay on their building footprints because several buildings share one large lot (for example blklot 8711507, about 12 acres).",
    "notes": "289-bed hospital complex (183-bed Benioff Children's Hospital, 36-bed Betty Irene Moore Women's Hospital, 70-bed Bakar Cancer Hospital), ~878,000 sq ft, ~$1.52 billion project cost. McDonough's project page credits Stantec (formerly Anshen+Allen) and William McDonough + Partners as architects; DPR's page credits Stantec Architecture. Opened Feb 1, 2015 (DPR) after over a decade of planning, design and construction.",
    "source_doc_urls": [
     "https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/580277612",
     "https://www.ucsfhealth.org/",
     "https://www.ucsf.edu/news/2014/11/121086/ucsf-medical-center-opens-15-billion-next-generation-hospital-complex-mission",
     "https://www.dpr.com/projects/ucsf-medical-center-at-mission-bay",
     "https://mcdonoughpartners.com/projects/ucsf-medical-center-at-mission-bay/"
    ]
   },
